      "problem": "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =6|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+7|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-2-0)-0+7(0-2) \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-2)+7\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-12-14 \\\\  & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$",
